		<p class="book-chapter-volume">Volume 2, Chapter 5</p><h1>Radicals and Reformers in the Progressive Era, 1900-1914</h1><div class="content-content">

<aside class="item" id="item-313">
<figure class="media-item preview-and-large-image">
<img class="large-image" src="https://www.whobuiltamerica.org/media/p2_5_1-rl.jpg" alt="These children were distributing socialist leaflets during a New York streetcar drivers&rsquo; strike in September 1916."><img class="preview-image" src="https://www.whobuiltamerica.org/media/p2_5_1-rm.jpg" alt="These children were distributing socialist leaflets during a New York streetcar drivers&rsquo; strike in September 1916."><svg class="view-expand-toggle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 100 100"><rect class="area" width="100" height="100"/><polygon class="handle" points="46.1 14.5 21.9 14.5 14.7 14.5 14.7 21.8 14.7 45.9 21.9 45.9 21.9 21.8 46.1 21.8 46.1 14.5"/><polygon class="handle" points="85.3 45.9 85.3 21.8 85.3 14.5 78.1 14.5 53.9 14.5 53.9 21.8 78.1 21.8 78.1 45.9 85.3 45.9"/><polygon class="handle" points="53.9 85.5 78.1 85.5 85.3 85.5 85.3 78.2 85.3 54.1 78.1 54.1 78.1 78.2 53.9 78.2 53.9 85.5"/><polygon class="handle" points="14.7 54.1 14.7 78.2 14.7 85.5 21.9 85.5 46.1 85.5 46.1 78.2 21.9 78.2 21.9 54.1 14.7 54.1"/><rect class="close" x="46.4" y="11.1" width="7.3" height="77.8" transform="translate(-20.7 50) rotate(-45)"/><rect class="close" x="11.1" y="46.4" width="77.8" height="7.3" transform="translate(-20.7 50) rotate(-45)"/></svg><figcaption class="media-item-caption"><h5>Solidarity and Skates</h5><p>These children were distributing socialist leaflets during a New York streetcar drivers’ strike in September 1916.</p><p class="source"><strong>Source:</strong> Prints and Photographs Division, Library of Congress, LC-DIG-ggbain-22868.
</p></figcaption></figure>
